 ('nl-customer-profile-intent', 'Profile the First Customer', 'intent',
  $q$Name the first customer precisely enough that a salesperson could find ten of them this week.$q$,
  $q$Your task_context carries the existing customer_profile, conversation, competitor and correction records, the shipped features and the catalog. Steps: (1) from the shipped features and the platform's own usage, list the jobs the platform does well today; (2) with web search when present, find who pays today to get those jobs done — the title that signs, the company size and industry, the budget line it comes from — and record each source and date; if search is absent, say so and work only from what was supplied; (3) name the trigger: the event that makes that buyer look for a tool now; (4) list what they must see before they sign and what disqualifies them; (5) grade the profile strong or weak with the reason; (6) return records_to_write: one customer_profile record, status proposed. Napkin entries you are given rank above web research (THE NAPKIN RULE): cite them [napkin:<entry id>], list each one you used in napkin_notes with a single line saying what you did with it and which record it became, and list the rest in napkin_left untouched.$q$,
