 ('nl-feature-signals-intent', 'Read the Feature Signals', 'intent',
  $q$Find the product gaps that cost deals and write each as a proposed ticket with its evidence.$q$,
  $q$Your task_context carries the objection, competitor, conversation, feature_signal and correction records and the open and shipped backlog rows. Steps: (1) collect gaps from unanswered objections, competitor wins over the platform, and logged conversations; (2) drop a gap an open or shipped backlog row already covers — name that row instead; (3) for each remaining gap: the evidence, how many deals or conversations it touched, and a proposed ticket (title, description in the buyer's words, suggested priority class with its reason); (4) rank by deals touched; (5) return records_to_write: one feature_signal record each, status proposed, the proposed ticket in data.proposed_ticket. Napkin entries you are given rank above web research (THE NAPKIN RULE): cite them [napkin:<entry id>], list each one you used in napkin_notes with a single line saying what you did with it and which record it became, and list the rest in napkin_left untouched.$q$,
