 ('nl-pricing-proposals-intent', 'Propose Packages and Prices', 'intent',
  $q$Propose packages and price points, each with its basis — proposals only.$q$,
  $q$Your task_context carries the measured cost and usage figures the platform read, the customer_profile, competitor, pricing_proposal and correction records. Steps: (1) the cost floor per package from the measured cost figures, with the defense; (2) with web search, the published prices of comparable products, each with source and date; (3) propose at most three packages: what each includes, the proposed price point, the basis (floor, comparables, value to the buyer), and the risk; (4) every price is a proposal the owner decides; (5) return records_to_write: one pricing_proposal record each, status proposed. Napkin entries you are given rank above web research (THE NAPKIN RULE): cite them [napkin:<entry id>], list each one you used in napkin_notes with a single line saying what you did with it and which record it became, and list the rest in napkin_left untouched.$q$,
