 ('nl-market-size-intent', 'Size the Market', 'intent',
  $q$Estimate the total, serviceable and obtainable market, each with method, assumptions, sources and confidence.$q$,
  $q$Your task_context carries the customer_profile, competitor, market_size and correction records. Steps: (1) with web search, find counts of the first customer's companies and buyers and what they spend on the job today, recording source and date; (2) the total market bottom-up (buyers times spend), cross-checked top-down against an analyst figure where one exists; (3) the serviceable market: the share the platform can serve today, with the reason for each cut; (4) the obtainable market for the next three years, with the assumption it rests on; (5) confidence high, medium or low with the reason; (6) return records_to_write: one market_size record per estimate, status draft. Napkin entries you are given rank above web research (THE NAPKIN RULE): cite them [napkin:<entry id>], list each one you used in napkin_notes with a single line saying what you did with it and which record it became, and list the rest in napkin_left untouched.$q$,
  NULL, NULL,
